## 7. Recommendations & Next Steps

1. **Stabilize the baseline detector output**  
   - Annotate a small held-out frame set (using `annotations/heldout_frames/`) via LabelMe, convert with `scripts/convert_labelme_annotations.py`, and run `scripts/eval_detections.py` to quantify precision/recall per class.  
   - Tune `config/thresholds.json` (or add per-class defaults to the TFJS pipeline) to curb the 200 detections/frame flood before layering trackers on top.

2. **Deliver the Day 1 3D viewer**  
   - Port the PLY rendering logic from `scripts/viewer_viser.py` into a Three.js component within `web/`, loading meshes from `web/assets/pointclouds/`.  
   - Co-locate the video overlay and 3D panel, even if they are not yet synchronized, to meet the first deliverable and unblock later pin rendering.

3. **Build the tracking + open-vocab pathway (Day 2 scope)**  
   - Choose a tracker (ByteTrack or BoT-SORT) in Python, associate detections across frames, and emit `outputs/tracks/pilot_plant_tracks.json` using the schema defined in the plan.  
   - Experiment with an OWL-ViT or GroundingDINO inference notebook to showcase zero-shot classes missing from the AutoML model; export the results alongside TFJS detections and add detector toggles in `web/main.js`.

4. **Invest in 3D localization tooling (Day 3 scope)**  
   - Stand up COLMAP or ORB-SLAM2 to recover camera intrinsics/extrinsics for `Pilot_plant.mp4`.  
   - Implement the alignment + ICP pipeline (Open3D or custom) to register SLAM output with `assets/pointclouds/pilot_plant_devices.ply`.  
   - Triangulate tracked centroids to produce `outputs/3d_pins/*.json`, record residual metrics, and feed them into the forthcoming Three.js scene.

5. **Extend the web app toward the “Ask Your Plant” experience (Day 4 scope)**  
   - Add an insights panel (counts per class, most confident detections) and search filters (e.g., highlight all hand valves).  
   - Prototype a text command input (even if stubbed) to frame the assistant story, and integrate track-based metadata (e.g., 3D coordinates from the upcoming pipeline).  
   - Document the demo steps, record a screen capture once the 3D sync exists, and start a slide deck referencing the metrics you compute.

6. **Housekeeping**  
   - Add missing Python dependencies (`opencv-python`, `trimesh`) to `requirements.txt`.  
   - Automate copying or symlinking `assets/` and `outputs/` into `web/` (or adjust the static server root) to avoid duplication drift.  
   - Expand `readme.md` with full setup instructions (virtualenv, frame sampling, inference, web preview) so reviewers can follow the workflow without guesswork.

Addressing the items above will move the project from “baseline detector” toward the complete hackathon vision described in the PDFs and PLAN.

